From 3e8d4be2a3717a420ef4b16bbb315b037275f104 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Juan=20Manuel=20L=C3=B3pez=20Carrillo?=
 <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 11:59:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 097/143] phy: allwinner: inno-combophy: register power
 notifier after probe success
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The power notifier (combphy->pwr_nb) was chained on
inno_subsys_notifier_list before the return value of
devm_of_phy_provider_register() was checked. On a probe failure the
struct sunxi_combphy is devm-freed but its notifier_block remains
chained, so the next inno_subsys power event dereferences freed memory
through container_of().

Register the notifier only after the provider has been published
successfully, and propagate the provider error immediately. This
matches the driver's own remove() path, which already pairs
atomic_notifier_chain_register() with an explicit unregister.

Signed-off-by: Juan Manuel López Carrillo <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/allwinner/sunxi-inno-combophy.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/allwinner/sunxi-inno-combophy.c b/drivers/phy/allwinner/sunxi-inno-combophy.c
index e37ca990d..ea2495044 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/allwinner/sunxi-inno-combophy.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/allwinner/sunxi-inno-combophy.c
@@ -1077,6 +1077,8 @@ static int sunxi_combphy_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	phy_set_drvdata(combphy->phy, combphy);
 
 	phy_provider = devm_of_phy_provider_register(dev, sunxi_combphy_xlate);
+	if (IS_ERR(phy_provider))
+		return PTR_ERR(phy_provider);
 
 	combphy->pwr_nb.notifier_call = sunxi_inno_combophy_power_event;
 	/* register inno power notifier */
@@ -1086,7 +1088,7 @@ static int sunxi_combphy_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	pm_runtime_enable(dev);
 	pm_runtime_get_sync(dev);
 
-	return PTR_ERR_OR_ZERO(phy_provider);
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static void sunxi_combphy_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
